    id: "live-audit-2026-11-03-price-first-line-own-name",
    agent: "knox",
    stage: "extract",
    lesson: "A line that opens with its price is named by the fee's own words right after that price, never by the whole line with its figures deleted. When the line prints a second figure (a waiver balance, a reduced price, a second fee), cut the name at the first clause boundary, waiver, condition, \"or\", \"per\" or \"for each\", past the price's own unit (\"$4.00 per month service charge\" is a service charge), and drop a bracket the cut leaves open. A monthly fee is named in the bank's words for it (\"Monthly fee\", \"Monthly service charge\"). A later price that opens a bracket after the first fee's words (\"($6 if age 55+)\") is a note on that fee, not a fee of its own, while a later price with its own fee words (\"$15.00 monthly fee without direct deposit\") still is. When those words name nothing, hold the line for review rather than invent a name. A name made by deleting figures reads as words the bank never printed, so the shared check cannot trace it and a reader sees nonsense; and when a rename fixes a whole class, queue the pages that carry it for one re-read so live fees take the new name.",
    why: "A live-site audit found Fort Worth City Credit Union's live 137329 named \"monthly fee, waived with minimum balance of or City of Fort Worth/City of Fort Worth Retirement direct deposit totalin\" from \"● $5 monthly fee, waived with minimum balance of $500 or ... totaling $500 or more\": the bullet left no words before the price, so the rules fell back to the whole line, deleted every amount and cut it at 120 characters, and the prose maintenance reader that names it \"Monthly fee\" ran only when no category was found. Of 534 live Knox fees read from price-first lines with a second figure (Nov 3, read-only), Knox v176 renames 251 at 166 institutions, none to a bare fee word, and loses none; 293 current-copy texts are queued for one re-read.",
